  "design": {
    "M": "32 ordinary/vector voices, local parameters/ADSR/pitch/mix/DSP, TF on actual M wiring, final sample schedule and HDMI/DAC; remote writes only via original PCM1 owner",
    "W": "Actual CNN/CQT/Viterbi, Classic HCI/SBC, bounded phone transport, sole C/BLE raw DDR recording object; no direct access to M TF/USB/DDR/HDMI/DAC",
    "policy": "PHONE_WINDOW_BLOCK defaults off. New explicit paired phone profiles select block PCM and capability version2/features0x80080601; legacy/new mixing cannot arm",
    "buffers": "W: one building plus one in-flight block, each at most five stereo32 words. M: one applied block. Bounded fail-closed waits; no audio sample backpressure",
    "barriers": "Posted local ACK means bounded queue admission; actual M completion ACK is an applied RAM watermark; all other original PCM1/clock commands wait for it. Original owner still checks key/bitmap/slot/COMMIT/SELECT",
    "failure": "Disconnect, wrong context, PANIC, overlap, overflow/malformed data and finite timeout revoke phone branch and stale history; local sample schedule independent",
    "contract": "rtl/workstation/TASK3_PHONE_WINDOW_CONTRACT.md"
  },
